From 4f635ab84a564bbb00838a776ef26e225d1e9780 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:43:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.6.1: host Submit Team, Music & Location in the
 room, Hidden Power IVs follow the named type

Host Submit Team (all platforms). The room's Submit Team button is now shown
to the host as well. The host's sheet takes a Showdown export or a
pokepast.es link, an in-game name and the host trainer model, and writes the
team straight into the GBA port 2 save that the room syncs at Start
(XDNetplay::SubmitHostTeam, sharing WriteSetsToSave with the guest path, whose
behaviour and status strings are unchanged). The room's format gate applies to
the host's paste too. With an imported save the write lands in the session's
disposable save and the import comes back when the room closes.

Music & Location (all platforms). A new host-only room button opens the
launcher's battle music and battle location lists (shared through
XDNetplay::StyleCombo on desktop) and rebuilds the synced Battle Style block
right away, so the picks apply at the next Start for both players.

Start safety. Start reads the host's saves and the Battle Style block and
sends them to the other player, so a late write would leave the two sides
booting different data. NetPlayServer::IsStartingOrRunning() (the two flags
are atomic now, and StartGame raises running before it clears pending) backs a
refusal on every one of these writes. Desktop checks it on the UI thread, the
thread Start reads on. Android serializes Start and the writes with one mutex
in the JNI layer, refuses once the room is closing (releasing the client and
the server waits on the same mutex), and greys the controls from the Start tap
on. The older Set Name control writes the same save and now follows the same
rules on every platform.

Hidden Power. Gen 3 and Gen 4 store no Hidden Power type; the game derives it
from IV parity. A paste that names a type ("Hidden Power [Ice]") but carries
no IVs, or only something like "IVs: 0 Atk", used to import as a different
type. The Showdown parser (C++ and the Android Kotlin port) now makes the IVs
match the named type: Showdown's standard spread when no IVs are given,
otherwise the fewest one-point changes, leaving stats the paste named alone
whenever possible. The spread table is checked against the type formula with a
static_assert.
